WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.800
In the first film, bringing two receptor kinases together released their brake and

2
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:08.800
activated the pair.

3
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:15.320
Yet one active receptor starts several pathways at once and also schedules its own

4
00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:21.760
shutoff. How can phosphotyrosines on one receptor pick different partners and end

5
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:22.760
signaling?

6
00:00:23.283 --> 00:00:28.583
Once switched on, the paired kinases add phosphates to tyrosines outside the

7
00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:35.023
catalytic core. In the epidermal growth factor receptor, most of those tyrosines sit

8
00:00:35.023 --> 00:00:36.383
along its flexible tails.

9
00:00:37.843 --> 00:00:43.143
Each newly phosphorylated tyrosine turns into a docking site for proteins floating

10
00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:44.143
in the cytosol.

11
00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:50.527
Inside the cell, signaling proteins read those marks with pockets called SH2

12
00:00:50.527 --> 00:00:55.607
domains. Such a pocket does not grab just any phosphotyrosine.

13
00:00:56.827 --> 00:01:00.987
It grips the phosphate and checks the few amino acids right after it.

14
00:01:02.147 --> 00:01:05.787
Mismatched proteins bounce away, while matching partners lock on.

15
00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:11.287
Watch how that local sequence splits one receptor into several pathways.

16
00:01:12.687 --> 00:01:17.547
One phosphotyrosine on the epidermal growth factor receptor tail carries an

17
00:01:17.547 --> 00:01:19.487
asparagine two residues later.

18
00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:25.047
That suits the adaptor Grb2, launching Ras and MAP kinase.

19
00:01:26.307 --> 00:01:31.847
Another site recruits PLC-gamma, an enzyme that splits a membrane lipid into two

20
00:01:31.847 --> 00:01:32.847
messengers.

21
00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:36.807
Swapping the receptor partner shifts the pathway mix.

22
00:01:38.107 --> 00:01:40.367
Remember violet HER3 from the first film.

23
00:01:41.687 --> 00:01:46.587
Its tail carries six tyrosines, each followed three residues later by methionine.

24
00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:53.287
Paired with HER2, those sites recruit PI 3-kinase, which drives the Akt growth and

25
00:01:53.287 --> 00:01:54.287
survival branch.

26
00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.160
Not every receptor puts all its docking sites on its own tail.

27
00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:05.360
Some use the stretch just under the membrane, or a loop inserted inside the kinase.

28
00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:11.620
The insulin receptor places many sites on separate adaptor proteins instead.

29
00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:16.080
Yet the same kind of sequence code still selects each partner.

30
00:02:17.183 --> 00:02:20.423
Here is the rule that organizes receptor output.

31
00:02:21.943 --> 00:02:26.803
Phosphotyrosines recruit specific partners by sequence to branch and end signaling.

32
00:02:28.163 --> 00:02:32.983
The tail even recruits its own removal tagger, the ubiquitin ligase Cbl.

33
00:02:34.483 --> 00:02:35.483
Pause and predict.

34
00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:41.243
If a mutant loses that Cbl docking site, what happens to the active receptor?

35
00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:50.827
It is removed more slowly, so it keeps signaling longer.

36
00:02:52.607 --> 00:02:55.727
Normally, Cbl docks there and attaches ubiquitin tags.

37
00:02:56.947 --> 00:03:02.527
The receptor is taken in by endocytosis, and those tags route it to the lysosome for

38
00:03:02.527 --> 00:03:08.427
digestion. Meanwhile, protein tyrosine phosphatases strip phosphates straight off

39
00:03:08.427 --> 00:03:10.987
the tail, erasing docking sites directly.

40
00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:16.787
One active receptor pair therefore acts like a sequence-coded switchboard.

41
00:03:18.247 --> 00:03:23.667
Kinases write phosphate marks, and neighboring amino acids largely decide whether a

42
00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:26.067
growth branch or a removal tagger lands.

43
00:03:27.447 --> 00:03:33.007
Together, tyrosine phosphatases and lysosomal digestion clear the board until the

44
00:03:33.007 --> 00:03:34.427
next growth factor arrives.
